*NOTE* - This README is obsolete and will be removed in future releases.
Please refer user guide for latest information

This file contains basic information on the port of U-Boot to TNETC550W.
All the changes fit in the common U-Boot infrastructure, providing a
new TNETC550W-specific entry in makefiles. 

New files:
----------

1. arm1176 support added as cpi/arm1176 by using existing arm1136 as base
2. The following new files have been added by this project:

board/tnetc550/                 - board-specific directory
board/tnetc550/Makefile	        - board-specific makefile
board/tnetc550/config.mk        - config file: defines TEXT_BASE, CROSS_COMPILE
board/tnetc550/flash.c	        - flash driver (for VOLCANO board)
board/tnetc550/u-boot.lds       - linker script
board/tnetc550/init_emif.S      - memory interface initialization
board/tnetc550/tnetc550.c       - board initialization
cpu/arm1176/cache.S	        - cache invlidate/flush routines
cpu/arm1176/Makefile	        - build rule for cache.S added
cpu/arm1176/puma5/              - SOC directory
cpu/arm1176/puma5/puma5.h       - puma5 registers and value masks
cpu/arm1176/puma5/timer.c       - puma5 timer 
cpu/arm1176/puma5/eth_cppi41.c  - CPPI4.1 based Ethernet Driver
cpu/arm1176/puma5/cpemacphy.c   - Ethernet Phy driver
cpu/arm1176/puma5/cpemacphy.h   - Phy configuration
cpu/arm1176/puma5/cppi41.h      - CPPI 4.1 
cpu/arm1176/puma5/mdio_reg.h    - MDIO map
cpu/arm1176/puma5/reset.S       - Reset control
cpu/arm1176/puma5/spansion.h    - Spansion flash configuration
cpu/arm1176/puma5/spi_sfi.h     - 
cpu/arm1176/puma5/spi_sfi.c     - 
cpu/arm1176/puma5/spi_sfi_client_info.c - 

include/configs/tnetc550.h      - main configuration file


Common file modifications:
--------------------------

The following common files have been modified by this project:
(starting from the ppcboot-0.9.3/ directory)

MAKEALL			- tnetc550 entry added
Makefile		- tnetc550_config entry added
cpu/arm1176/start.S	- reset_cpu is made SOC specific for CONFIG_TNETC550


Board specific Configuration options:
------------------------------------

CONFIG_TNETC550

	Main board-specific option (should be defined for TNETC550W and derived
        builds).

CONFIG_PUMA5_QT_EMU

	Gives TNETC550W derived build for puma5 on Quickturn Emulation platform.
        
CONFIG_PUMA5_VOLCANO_EMU

	Gives TNETC550W derived build for puma5 on VOLCANO Emulation platform.


Build U-Boot for TNETC550W
---------------------------
1. U-Boot build uses CROSS_COMPILE variable to determine toolchain
   prefix. The TNETC550W build defines prefix as "arm_v6_be_uclibc-". Any other
   toolchain prefix needs to be either exported as shell environment or
   explicitly provided as argument to 'make'.  
2. To configure TNETC550W build, type 
   "make tnetc550_config" at shell for board having serial flash of  64KB sector size.
   "make tnetc550_sect_256K_config" at shell for board having serial flash of 256KB sector size.
   Alternatively,   
    - For Volcano build, use 'make tnetc550_volcano_config'
    - For Volcano build with SPI Flash, use 'make
      tnetc550_volcano_spiflash_config'.
    - For Quickturn build, use 'make tnetc550_qt_config'
3. Edit the "include/configs/tnetc550.h" file if necessary to change/add
   configurations (please read limitations/known issues section below), 
4. type "make"



Limitations/Known Issues
------------------------
1. Added flag -mno-thumb-interwork as PLATFORM_CPPFLAGS in
   board/tnetc550/config.mk to avoid warning


Linux boot configurations
-------------------------
U-Boot is configured to be located @81FF0000 in RAM (Top), so Linux and
Ramdisk (if any) should be loaded accordingly. By default U-Boot expects Linux
image in uImage format to boot. In addition U-Boot for tnetc550 supports UBFI image to boot
(please refer "Design Document - U-Boot Dual Image Support.doc" 
for UBFI image details).

A) Booting uImage
-----------------
The Linux image can be converted to U-Boot uImage format by using the 'mkimage'
tool (from psp_uboot/tools directory). For example, following command builds
uImage from zImage: 
    mkimage -A arm -O linux -T kernel -C none -a 80a00000 -e 80a00000 -n "Linux Kernel Image" -d zImage uImage

Refer to README file in U-Boot source directory for additional details to build
uImage.  

After flashing Linux (and if used, putting Ramdisk in RAM), the U-Boot
'bootargs' environment variable should be set similar to below examples:

1. Boot Linux with Ramdisk - 
   Assuming flash map 
            U-Boot @48000000
            Environment sectors of Size = 64KB each
            Linux @48100000
            Root FS @48300000
            
   'bootargs' for Linux with ramdisk @80400000 in RAM are set as,
  
   => setenv bootargs 'root=/dev/ram initrd=0x80400000,<ramdisk-size>  mtdparts=physmap-flash.0:128k@0x000000(U-Boot)ro,64k(env1),64k(env2),2m(Kernel),3m(RootFileSystem) console=ttyS0,38400n8'

   Here ramdisk-size needs to be filled as per the size of ramdisk.  

2. Boot Linux with squashfs in Serial flash - 
   => setenv bootargs 'root=/dev/mtdblock5 mtdparts=spansion:128k@0x000000(U-Boot)ro,64k(env1),64k(env2),2m(Kernel),2m(RootFileSystem) console=ttyS0,38400n8'

After the above settings, 'bootm <linux-img-addr>' command at U-Boot prompt
should boot the kernel.

B) Booting UBFI
---------------
Please refer "Building UBFI" section below to build ubfi image. 

The Current U-Boot build uses two 3.7MB fixed partitions for UBFI images starting
@256KB offset from FLASH base. In default (initial) configuration, image in
partition 1 is booted.  So, assuming flash base as 48000000, the map would be:
    U-Boot @48000000
    UBFI1 @48040000
    UBFI2 @483F0000

U-Boot built in 'update' script could be used to download (using tftp) and flash
the ubfi image. By default ubfi image 1 name is assumed to be 'bootImage1' but
can be changed by 'setenv UBFINAME1 <name>'

In addition IP environment variables need to be set before running the script.
Please refer "Using TFTP" section.

Use 'run update1' to flash UBFI1 or 'run update2' to flash UBFI2.

The default 'bootcmd' includes a script to automatically configure and boot UBFI
image so just typing 'boot' at U-Boot prompt should boot the kernel.


Building UBFI Image
---------------------
Use 'mkubfi' script in psp_uboot/tools directory to build the UBFI image as
described below:

1) Prepare kernel image (e.g., zImage) and File-system (e.g.,
puma5-lzma-squashfs.img) and any other images (optional) required to build UBFI
image. 

2) Build 'mkimage' tool from U-Boot if it is not already built. Use following
commad sequence in U-Boot base directory (u-boot-1.2.0) at Linux shell: 

    make tnetc550_config 
	for board having serial flash of  64KB sector size.
    make tnetc550_sect_256K_config 
	for board having serial flash of 256KB sector size.
	and 
    make tools
    
Note that generally this tool gets built when building U-Boot.

3) The 'mkubfi' scripts expects 'mkimage' executable to be in PATH. e.g. to use
'mkimage' built in above step, add following path:- /vobs/psp_uboot/tools/ubfi/

4) Make sure that the bootscript (bootscript.txt) is available. By default this
file is already present in the 'mkubfi' directory in clearcase VOB. 

5) The bootscript can be modified to change image/partion configurations. For
this, the configuration values at top of the bootscript need to be edited.
Currently supported configurations are:
    i)      Flash device - 'flash_bootdev' indicates Flash device used for
    booting. For Parallel flash use 'flash_bootdev=physmap-flash.0' and Serial
    flash, use 'flash_bootdev=spansion'.

    ii)    Setting flag 'boot_flash' - Make sure to set the flag
    'boot_flash=1' when a board has two flashes (e.g., both parallel and
    serial flash) and using second flash as boot flash. In case using only one
    or first flash to store U-Boot as well as UBFI images, set 'boot_flash' to
    '0'. 
    
    For any other configuration, modify the bootscript.txt file to have
    correct 'rootinfo'.
    
    iii)    Additional MTD partitions - Provide mtd partitions as
    'mtdparts_extra'. Note that a comma (',') must be included at start. For
    example, 'mtdparts_extra=,1M@7M(DUMMY)'.  

    In case no additional partitions are required, mtdparts_extra should be set
    as empty, e.g, default 'mtdparts_extra='.

    iv)     Additional boot arguments - Additional information needed by Linux
    can be passed through defining 'bootargs_extra' which will be appended to
    'bootargs'. For example, 'bootargs_extra=ethaddr0=${ethaddr}'.

6) Run 'mkubfi' at shell, it is required that bootscript, kernel and filesystem
are passed at fixed argument position to mkubfi as shown below:
    mkubfi <blocksize[KB|MB]> <linux-load-addr> <bootscript-name> <linuximg-name> <fsimg-name> <additional-files...> 

Here, 'blocksize' should be passed as (or multiple of) erase block size of the
flash used. 

For example, assuming all the file components of UBFI image are in current
    directory as 'mkubfi', 
    mkubfi 64kb 80a00000 bootscript.txt zImage puma5-lzma-squashfs.img


Using TFTP
-----------
U-Boot has support for downloading the files over ethernet using 'tftpboot'
command. This requires setting the following environment variables: 

setenv ethaddr aa.bb.cc.11.22.33 (optional)
setenv ipaddr 172.24.190.166
setenv serverip 172.24.133.60
setenv gatewayip 172.24.182.2
setenv netmask 255.255.252.0

Note that ethernet link is only up when 'tftpboot' command is given and is shut
down again after the download finishes/aborts.


Flash Layout
-------------
The layouts consider two UBFI partitions in Flash.

Note: If case of any change in UBFI positions, refer "UBFI Partion Change"
section below.

            NOR Flash Map (32MB)                                                  
            =====================

        +-----------------------+    3800_0000
        |                       |
        |        U-Boot         |
        |        (512KB)        |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    3808_0000
        |        Env1           |
        |        (256KB)        |
        +-----------------------+    380C_0000
        |        Env2           |
        |        (256KB)        |
        +-----------------------+    3810_0000
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |        UBFI1          |
        |        (5MB)          |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    3860_0000
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |        UBFI2          |
        |        (5MB)          |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    38B0_0000
        |                       |
        |       (spare)         |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    39FF_FFFF



       Serial (MM-SPI) Flash Map (8MB) 
       ==============================

        +-----------------------+    4800_0000
        |                       |
        |        U-Boot         |
        |        (128KB)        |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    4802_0000
        |        Env1           |
        |        (64KB)         |
        +-----------------------+    4803_0000
        |        Env2           |
        |        (64KB)         |
        +-----------------------+    4804_0000
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |        UBFI1          |
        |        (3.687MB)      |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    483F_0000
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |        UBFI2          |
        |        (3.687MB)      |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    487A_0000
        |                       |
        |       (spare)         |
        |                       |
        +-----------------------+    487F_FFFF



UBFI Partitions Change
-----------------------
There are two ways to update UBFI partions definition:

1) Erase both the environment sectors and rebuild U-Boot by changing following
#defines: 
    UBFI1_SECT_BASE
    UBFI2_SECT_BASE

OR
2) Go to U-Boot prompt and use following commands:
    setenv UBFIADDR1 <new UBFI1 address>
    setenv UBFIADDR2 <new UBFI2 address>
    saveenv

In case if the "update1" and "update2" scripts are needed, they need to be
modified to use new addresses.



